1. How to reduce latency issue in Gen-AI Application -: ----------------------------  ✅
“Latency in Gen‑AI apps comes from both model inference and retrieval. To reduce it, we can optimize the model (smaller, quantized, batched), streamline retrieval (efficient chunking, tuned vector stores, caching), and architect the system for speed (async calls, streaming, autoscaling). In practice, combining caching with streaming responses gives the biggest user‑perceived improvement.”


2. Different stretegy about chunking -- ------------------------  ✅

“Chunking is critical in RAG pipelines because embeddings work best on semantically coherent text. Fixed‑size chunking is simple but can break meaning. Recursive chunking preserves structure by splitting at natural boundaries. Overlap ensures context isn’t lost between chunks. Semantic chunking is the most advanced, using NLP to split by meaning. The choice depends on the data type and retrieval needs.”

